puts N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 16."],"tables":[]},{"name":"LSub","category":"Math","group":"","title":"Difference of Long values","formula":"Y = A - B","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["A","input","Long","A","First operand","0"],["B","input","Long","B","Second operand","0"],["Y","output","Long","Y","Result of operation Y=A-B","-"]],"notes":["The module subtracts the value of input B from the value of input A and stores the result in output Y. Y=A-B"],"tables":[]},{"name":"LXor","category":"Math","group":"","title":"Bitwise XOR of Long values","formula":"Y = X0 xor X1 ...","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X0","input","Long","X0","First operand","0"],["X1","input","Long","X1","Second operand","0"],["Y","output","Long","Y","Result of operation Y = X0 ^ X1","-"]],"notes":["The module computes the exclusive OR of the individual bits of the values X0 and X1 and stores the result in output Y. Y = X0 ^ X1","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 16."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Mean","category":"Math","group":"","title":"Arithmetic mean","formula":"Calculates mean of X every time is triggered.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Tr","input","Boolean","Trigger","Enables the value X to be included in the average","0"],["X","input","Int","X","Input value","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Current arithmetic mean of the included values","-"]],"notes":["If the value on input Tr is 1, the value of input X is stored into an internal buffer. The arithmetic mean of the values stored in this buffer is computed and the result is stored in output Y.","The buffer size (i.e. the number of averaged values) is configurable. The display of the module's internal buffer pins can also be enabled, for example in order to store them in FRAM memory with the SaveData module.","The default size is 12 values."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Sar","category":"Math","group":"","title":"Arithmetic right shift of the bits of a Long value","formula":"Y = X >> B","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Long","X","Input value","0"],["B","input","Int","B","Number of bits to shift","0"],["Y","output","Long","Y","Result of operation Y = X >> B","-"]],"notes":["The module computes an arithmetic right shift of the individual bits of the value X while preserving the sign and stores the result in output Y. The highest B bits of the result Y contain a copy of the highest bit of the value on input X. Y = X >> B"],"tables":[]},{"name":"Shl","category":"Math","group":"","title":"Logical left shift of the bits of a Long value","formula":"Y = X << B","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Long","X","Input value","0"],["B","input","Int","B","Number of bits to shift","0"],["Y","output","Long","Y","Result of operation Y = X << B","-"]],"notes":["The module computes a logical left shift of the individual bits of the value X and stores the result in output Y. The lowest B bits of the result Y are cleared. Y = X << B"],"tables":[]},{"name":"2xAO","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Sets 2 analog outputs of the PLC","formula":"Sets analog outputs","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["AO0","input","Int","AO 0","Value of analog output AO 0","0"],["AO1","input","Int","AO 1","Value of analog output AO 1","0"]],"notes":["The module writes the configured values of inputs AO0 and AO1 to the corresponding PLC outputs."],"tables":[]},{"name":"8xAI","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads 8 analog inputs of the PLC","formula":"Returns analog input. Emulate by \"12345678\" and \"QWERTYUI\" keys","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["AI0","output","Int","AI 0","Value of analog input AI 0","-"],["AI1","output","Int","AI 1","Value of analog input AI 1","-"],["AI2","output","Int","AI 2","Value of analog input AI 2","-"],["AI3","output","Int","AI 3","Value of analog input AI 3","-"],["AI4","output","Int","AI 4","Value of analog input AI 4","-"],["AI5","output","Int","AI 5","Value of analog input AI 5","-"],["AI6","output","Int","AI 6","Value of analog input AI 6","-"],["AI7","output","Int","AI 7","Value of analog input AI 7","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the values of the PLC analog inputs and stores them in the corresponding outputs AI0 to AI7.","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the values AI0 to AI7 can be increased with the keys 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 and 8 and decreased with the keys Q W E R T Y U and I."],"tables":[]},{"name":"8xDI","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads 8 binary inputs of the PLC","formula":"Returns digital input. Emulate by \"ASDFGHJK\" keys.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["DI0","output","Boolean","DI 0","Value of binary input DI 0","-"],["DI1","output","Boolean","DI 1","Value of binary input DI 1","-"],["DI2","output","Boolean","DI 2","Value of binary input DI 2","-"],["DI3","output","Boolean","DI 3","Value of binary input DI 3","-"],["DI4","output","Boolean","DI 4","Value of binary input DI 4","-"],["DI5","output","Boolean","DI 5","Value of binary input DI 5","-"],["DI6","output","Boolean","DI 6","Value of binary input DI 6","-"],["DI7","output","Boolean","DI 7","Value of binary input DI 7","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the values of the PLC binary inputs and stores them in the corresponding outputs DI0 to DI7.","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the values DI0 to DI7 can be toggled from 0 to 1 and back with the keys A S D F G H J and K."],"tables":[]},{"name":"8xDO","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Sets 8 binary outputs of the PLC","formula":"Sets digital outputs","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["DO0","input","Boolean","DO 0","Value of binary output DO 0","0"],["DO1","input","Boolean","DO 1","Value of binary output DO 1","0"],["DO2","input","Boolean","DO 2","Value of binary output DO 2","0"],["DO3","input","Boolean","DO 3","Value of binary output DO 3","0"],["DO4","input","Boolean","DO 4","Value of binary output DO 4","0"],["DO5","input","Boolean","DO 5","Value of binary output DO 5","0"],["DO6","input","Boolean","DO 6","Value of binary output DO 6","0"],["DO7","input","Boolean","DO 7","Value of binary output DO 7","0"]],"notes":["The module writes the configured values of inputs DO0 to DO7 to the corresponding PLC outputs."],"tables":[]},{"name":"8xPWM","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Sets 8 PWM outputs of the PLC","formula":"Sets PWM outputs","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["AO0","input","Int","AO 0","Value of modulated output DO 0","0"],["AO1","input","Int","AO 1","Value of modulated output DO 1","0"],["AO2","input","Int","AO 2","Value of modulated output DO 2","0"],["AO3","input","Int","AO 3","Value of modulated output DO 3","0"],["AO4","input","Int","AO 4","Value of modulated output DO 4","0"],["AO5","input","Int","AO 5","Value of modulated output DO 5","0"],["AO6","input","Int","AO 6","Value of modulated output DO 6","0"],["AO7","input","Int","AO 7","Value of modulated output DO 7","0"]],"notes":["The module pulse-width modulates the configured values of inputs AO0 to AO7 onto the corresponding PLC outputs. The working range of the values on the AOx inputs is 0 - N, where N is the number of steps (256 by default, changeable in the module configuration). If the input value is <= 0 the output is permanently off. If the input value is >= N the output is permanently on. For values X = (1 to N-1) the output is modulated so that it is on for X steps and off for (N-X) steps of the PWM module.","The output works in PWM mode when the corresponding logic output of the 8xDO module is set to 0. When the input of the 8xDO module has the value 1, the output is permanently on.","Output state as a function of the input value of the 8xPWM and 8xDO modules:","In the module configuration dialog the number of PWM steps N and the corresponding frequency and period of the signal on the outputs can be set."],"tables":[{"head":["Hodnota PWM vstupu X (PWM value of input X)","Hodnota vstupu modulu 8xDO (Input value of the 8xDO module)","Stav výstupu (Output state)"],"rows":[["X <= 0","0","0"],["1 ÷ N-1","0","Střída X / N"],["X >= N","0","1"],["Libovolná","1","1"]]}]},{"name":"Cnt","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the PLC counter values","formula":"Internal counter. Emulate by \"+\", \"-\" keys","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Ch","input","Int","Channel","Channel number of the counter","0"],["Cnt","output","Long","Counter","Counter value","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the counter value on channel Ch. The meaning of the channel number depends on the module type. A description of the individual modules follows.","These modules allow unidirectional and bidirectional counters on the digital inputs DI0-7 to be processed, the period on those inputs to be measured, and pulses on the analog inputs AI0-7 to be counted.","Channels 0 to 7 act as pulse counters on PLC inputs DI0 to DI7. Channels 8-11 act as bidirectional counters suitable for connecting an IRC (incremental encoder) sensor. For the phases connected to DI0 and DI1 use channel 8. Similarly for the phases connected to DI2 and DI3 use channel 9, for the phases on DI4 and DI5 channel 10, and finally the phases on DI6 and DI7 affect channel 11.","Channels 20 - 27 act as pulse counters on PLC analog inputs AI0 to AI7. A voltage >= 50% of the input range counts as logical 1, a voltage < 25% of the range counts as logical 0; the input hysteresis is therefore 25% of the range. The inputs are sampled at 100 Hz.","The module can also measure the period of the input signals of counters 0 to 7 when a channel number in the range 12 to 19 is selected. The period value on output Cnt is in the range 0 - 0xFF00; for longer periods the output value stops at that maximum. The time unit of the period is determined by the firmware version. At the time this documentation was written, the following firmware versions supported period measurement:","Plc_P3+Slow","1 / 1200 s","833.3 μs","Plc_P3+","1 / 7200 s","138.9 μs","Plc_P3+Fast","1 / 28800 s","34.7 μs","This module allows pulses to be counted on analog inputs 0-3. The channel number must be in the range 0-3. The voltage levels for logical 1 and 0 are the same as for the P3 module, i.e. 50% and 25% of the input range.","Note: If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the value of output Cnt can be changed with the + and - keys."],"tables":[{"head":["Jméno (Name)","Jednotka periody (Period unit)","Rozlišení (Resolution)","Maximální perioda (Maximum period)"],"rows":[["Plc_P3+Slow","1 / 1200 s","833,3 μs","54,4 s"],["Plc_P3+","1 / 7200 s","138,9 μs","9,07 s"],["Plc_P3+Fast","1 / 28800 s","34,7 μs","2,27 s"]]}]},{"name":"IIC_16xAI","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the inputs of an IIC card with 16 analog inputs","formula":"Returns 16 IIC analog inputs. Emulate by \"QWERTYUI\", \"ASDFGHJK\" and Shift keys.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"],["AI0","output","Int","AI 0","Value of analog input AI 0","-"],["AI1","output","Int","AI 1","Value of analog input AI 1","-"],["AI2","output","Int","AI 2","Value of analog input AI 2","-"],["AI3","output","Int","AI 3","Value of analog input AI 3","-"],["AI4","output","Int","AI 4","Value of analog input AI 4","-"],["AI5","output","Int","AI 5","Value of analog input AI 5","-"],["AI6","output","Int","AI 6","Value of analog input AI 6","-"],["AI7","output","Int","AI 7","Value of analog input AI 7","-"],["AI8","output","Int","AI 8","Value of analog input AI 8","-"],["AI9","output","Int","AI 9","Value of analog input AI 9","-"],["AI10","output","Int","AI 10","Value of analog input AI 10","-"],["AI11","output","Int","AI 11","Value of analog input AI 11","-"],["AI12","output","Int","AI 12","Value of analog input AI 12","-"],["AI13","output","Int","AI 13","Value of analog input AI 13","-"],["AI14","output","Int","AI 14","Value of analog input AI 14","-"],["AI15","output","Int","AI 15","Value of analog input AI 15","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the values of the analog inputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus and stores them in the corresponding outputs AI0 to AI15.","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the values AI0 to AI7 can be increased with the keys Q W E R T Y U and I and decreased with the keys A S D F G H J and K. Using the same keys together with the Shift modifier you can change the values of inputs AI8 to AI15"],"tables":[]},{"name":"IIC_3xDO","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Sets the outputs of an IIC card with 3 binary outputs","formula":"Sets 3 IIC digital outputs","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["DO0","input","Boolean","DO 0","Value of binary output DO 0","0"],["DO1","input","Boolean","DO 1","Value of binary output DO 1","0"],["DO2","input","Boolean","DO 2","Value of binary output DO 2","0"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"]],"notes":["The module writes the configured values of inputs DO0 to DO2 to the corresponding outputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IIC_8xAI","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the inputs of an IIC card with 8 analog inputs","formula":"Returns 8 IIC analog inputs. Emulate by \"QWERTYUI\" and \"ASDFGHJK\" keys.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"],["AI0","output","Int","AI 0","Value of analog input AI 0","-"],["AI1","output","Int","AI 1","Value of analog input AI 1","-"],["AI2","output","Int","AI 2","Value of analog input AI 2","-"],["AI3","output","Int","AI 3","Value of analog input AI 3","-"],["AI4","output","Int","AI 4","Value of analog input AI 4","-"],["AI5","output","Int","AI 5","Value of analog input AI 5","-"],["AI6","output","Int","AI 6","Value of analog input AI 6","-"],["AI7","output","Int","AI 7","Value of analog input AI 7","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the values of the analog inputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus and stores them in the corresponding outputs AI0 to AI7.","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the values AI0 to AI7 can be increased with the keys Q W E R T Y U and I and decreased with the keys A S D F G H J and K."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IIC_8xAO","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Sets the outputs of an IIC card with 8 analog outputs","formula":"Sets 8 IIC analog outputs","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["AO0","input","Int","AO 0","Value of analog output AO 0","0"],["AO1","input","Int","AO 1","Value of analog output AO 1","0"],["AO2","input","Int","AO 2","Value of analog output AO 2","0"],["AO3","input","Int","AO 3","Value of analog output AO 3","0"],["AO4","input","Int","AO 4","Value of analog output AO 4","0"],["AO5","input","Int","AO 5","Value of analog output AO 5","0"],["AO6","input","Int","AO 6","Value of analog output AO 6","0"],["AO7","input","Int","AO 7","Value of analog output AO 7","0"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"]],"notes":["The module writes the configured values of inputs AO0 to AO7 to the corresponding outputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IIC_8xDO","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Sets the outputs of an IIC card with 8 binary outputs","formula":"Sets 8 IIC digital outputs","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["DO0","input","Boolean","DO 0","Value of binary output DO 0","0"],["DO1","input","Boolean","DO 1","Value of binary output DO 1","0"],["DO2","input","Boolean","DO 2","Value of binary output DO 2","0"],["DO3","input","Boolean","DO 3","Value of binary output DO 3","0"],["DO4","input","Boolean","DO 4","Value of binary output DO 4","0"],["DO5","input","Boolean","DO 5","Value of binary output DO 5","0"],["DO6","input","Boolean","DO 6","Value of binary output DO 6","0"],["DO7","input","Boolean","DO 7","Value of binary output DO 7","0"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"]],"notes":["The module writes the configured values of inputs DO0 to DO7 to the corresponding outputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IIC_9xDI","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the inputs of an IIC card with 9 binary inputs","formula":"Returns 9 IIC digital input. Emulate by \"ASDFGHJKL\" keys.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"],["DI0","output","Boolean","DI 0","Value of binary input DI 0","-"],["DI1","output","Boolean","DI 1","Value of binary input DI 1","-"],["DI2","output","Boolean","DI 2","Value of binary input DI 2","-"],["DI3","output","Boolean","DI 3","Value of binary input DI 3","-"],["DI4","output","Boolean","DI 4","Value of binary input DI 4","-"],["DI5","output","Boolean","DI 5","Value of binary input DI 5","-"],["DI6","output","Boolean","DI 6","Value of binary input DI 6","-"],["DI7","output","Boolean","DI 7","Value of binary input DI 7","-"],["DI8","output","Boolean","DI 8","Value of binary input DI 8","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the values of the binary inputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus and stores them in the corresponding outputs DI0 to DI8.","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the values DI0 to DI8 can be toggled from 0 to 1 and back with the keys A S D F G H J K and L."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IIC_9xDICnt","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the inputs and counter values of an IIC card with 9 binary inputs","formula":"Returns 9 IIC digital input with counters. Emulate by \"ASDFGHJKL\" keys.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Address of the module on the IIC bus","0"],["DI0","output","Boolean","DI 0","Value of binary input DI 0","-"],["DI1","output","Boolean","DI 1","Value of binary input DI 1","-"],["DI2","output","Boolean","DI 2","Value of binary input DI 2","-"],["DI3","output","Boolean","DI 3","Value of binary input DI 3","-"],["DI4","output","Boolean","DI 4","Value of binary input DI 4","-"],["DI5","output","Boolean","DI 5","Value of binary input DI 5","-"],["DI6","output","Boolean","DI 6","Value of binary input DI 6","-"],["DI7","output","Boolean","DI 7","Value of binary input DI 7","-"],["DI8","output","Boolean","DI 8","Value of binary input DI 8","-"],["Cnt0","output","Word","Counter 0","Pulse counter value on input DI 0","-"],["Cnt1","output","Word","Counter 1","Pulse counter value on input DI 1","-"],["Cnt2","output","Word","Counter 2","Pulse counter value on input DI 2","-"],["Cnt3","output","Word","Counter 3","Pulse counter value on input DI 3","-"],["Cnt4","output","Word","Counter 4","Pulse counter value on input DI 4","-"],["Cnt5","output","Word","Counter 5","Pulse counter value on input DI 5","-"],["Cnt6","output","Word","Counter 6","Pulse counter value on input DI 6","-"],["Cnt7","output","Word","Counter 7","Pulse counter value on input DI 7","-"],["Cnt8","output","Word","Counter 8","Pulse counter value on input DI 8","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the values of the binary inputs of the card with address Addr on the IIC bus and stores them in the corresponding outputs DI0 to DI8. In addition it reads the pulse counter values on the individual inputs and stores them in the corresponding outputs Cnt0 to Cnt8.","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the values DI0 to DI8 can be toggled from 0 to 1 and back with the keys A S D F G H J K and L. Simulated pulses are also reflected in the corresponding counters."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IRC","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Processes a connected IRC (incremental encoder) sensor","formula":"Incremental counter. Emulate by \"+\", \"-\" keys","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Sync","input","Boolean","Synchronize","If =1, Cnt is synchronised with Null","0"],["Cnt","output","Long","Counter","Counter value","-"],["Null","output","Int","NullCounter","Counter value cleared by the null pulse","-"]],"notes":["The module processes an IRC (incremental encoder) sensor connected to the PLC binary inputs (phase 1 on DI6, phase 2 on DI7 and the zero pulse on DI5).","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the counter value can be changed with the + and - keys."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ReadAI","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the values of the PLC analog inputs","formula":"Read single analog channel. Emulate by \"+\", \"-\" keys","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Ch","input","Int","Channel","Channel number of the analog input","0"],["Out","output","Int","Output","Value of the input","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the counter value on channel Ch. Each analog input can be read as a slow or a fast input. Slow inputs have even channel numbers 0, 2, 4, ... 14. Fast inputs have odd channel numbers 1, 3, 5, ... 15.","In the current FW version the slow inputs are averaged from 64 samples and are refreshed with a period of 640 ms. The fast inputs are averaged from 8 samples and are refreshed with a period of 80 ms (12.5 Hz).","If the module is selected while the simulation is running, the value of output Cnt can be changed with the + and - keys."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ReadDallas","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Reads the temperature value from a Dallas DS18B20 thermometer","formula":"Reads temperature from Dallas DS18B20.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Code","parameter","Long","Rom Code","Unique code of the thermometer","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"],["T","output","Int","Temperature","Temperature read","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the temperature from a single Dallas DS18B20 thermometer identified by the unique code on the Code input. The temperature read is stored in output T. Output St shows the read status (=1..success, =0..read failed)","This module should be used in the \"Timer 1s\" process!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"StepDriver","category":"I/O","group":"","title":"Controls a stepper motor by generating CLK and DIR pulses","formula":"Controls step driver.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Start","input","Boolean","Start","Starts the motor movement towards the position given by the Posit input","0"],["Preset","input","Boolean","Preset","Sets the motor position (output Pos) to the value of input PrPos. Can only be performed while the motor is standing (output Run = 0).","0"],["Speed","input","Int","Speed","Requested motor speed. Range: 0-255. A value of 0 stops the movement. Unit: 10 Hz, so the maximum frequency is 2550 steps/s.","0"],["StartS","input","Int","Start Speed","Initial speed value. The given acceleration (ramp) applies from this speed upwards.","32"],["Accel","input","Int","Acceleration","Requested steepness of the speed ramp. Range: 1-255. A higher value means a steeper acceleration and braking.","64"],["Posit","input","Long","Position","Requested target motor position. Used when the Start input = 1.","0"],["PrPos","input","Long","Preset Pos.","Position preset for the Preset operation.","0"],["Run","output","Boolean","Run","If the motor is running, output Run has the value 1.","-"],["Spd","output","Int","Actual speed","Instantaneous speed value.","-"],["Pos","output","Long","Actual pos.","Instantaneous motor position.","-"]],"notes":["Int","The module controls a stepper motor using CLK pulses and the DIR direction signal (on the P3+ unit these are outputs Out0 and Out1).","The individual commands are controlled by the logical inputs En, Start and Preset as follows:","If the En input is active, the values on the Speed, StartS and Accel inputs are applied on every execution of this block and all 3 outputs are updated. This allows the movement speed to be changed while the motor is running. The actual speed approaches the requested speed on input Speed with acceleration Accel. The acceleration only takes effect at speeds above StartSpeed. If the requested speed on input Speed is zero, the movement stops (after the ramp) and output Run then goes to 0.","The Start input starts the motor moving from the current position Pos to the target position given by the Posit input. If the motor was already moving (Run=1), the target position is updated. If that target position requires a change of direction, the motor is stopped (along the given ramp) and started in the opposite direction.","The Preset input allows the current position on output Pos to be overwritten with the value on the PrPos input. This can only be done while the motor is not moving (output Run = 0). It is used when calibrating the motor position by moving to a known point and writing the position of that point to output Pos."],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NRFloat","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Reads a float value from the D3-Net network","formula":"Reads float value from D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Variable identifier","512"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously reads a variable from the D3-Net network, specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This reading takes place in the background. After a successful read the value is stored in an internal buffer and a logical 1 appears on output St. This output should be connected to the En input of the StoreFloatData module, which makes the value from the internal buffer available for further processing.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NRFloatMtx","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Reads a matrix of float values from the D3-Net network","formula":"Reads float matrix from D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Matrix identifier","512"],["Row","parameter","Int","Row","Row number in the matrix","0"],["Rows","parameter","Int","Rows","Number of rows read","0"],["Col","parameter","Int","Column","Column number in the matrix","0"],["Cols","parameter","Int","Columns","Number of columns read","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously reads a matrix or part of it from the D3-Net network. The matrix of values is specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This reading takes place in the background. After a successful read the value is stored in an internal buffer and a logical 1 appears on output St. This output should be connected to the En input of the StoreFloatData module, which makes the values from the internal buffer available for further processing.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NRInt","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Reads an int value from the D3-Net network","formula":"Reads int value from D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Variable identifier","510"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously reads a variable from the D3-Net network, specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This reading takes place in the background. After a successful read the value is stored in an internal buffer and a logical 1 appears on output St. This output should be connected to the En input of the StoreIntData module, which makes the value from the internal buffer available for further processing.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NRIntMtx","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Reads a matrix of int values from the D3-Net network","formula":"Reads int matrix from D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Matrix identifier","510"],["Row","parameter","Int","Row","Row number in the matrix","0"],["Rows","parameter","Int","Rows","Number of rows read","0"],["Col","parameter","Int","Column","Column number in the matrix","0"],["Cols","parameter","Int","Columns","Number of columns read","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously reads a matrix or part of it from the D3-Net network. The matrix of values is specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This reading takes place in the background. After a successful read the value is stored in an internal buffer and a logical 1 appears on output St. This output should be connected to the En input of the StoreIntData module, which makes the values from the internal buffer available for further processing.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NRLong","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Reads a long value from the D3-Net network","formula":"Reads long value from D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Variable identifier","511"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously reads a variable from the D3-Net network, specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This reading takes place in the background. After a successful read the value is stored in an internal buffer and a logical 1 appears on output St. This output should be connected to the En input of the StoreLongData module, which makes the value from the internal buffer available for further processing.","If the WID input is set to -1, the system time of the station specified by the Addr input is read.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NRLongMtx","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Reads a matrix of long values from the D3-Net network","formula":"Reads long matrix from D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Matrix identifier","511"],["Row","parameter","Int","Row","Row number in the matrix","0"],["Rows","parameter","Int","Rows","Number of rows read","0"],["Col","parameter","Int","Column","Column number in the matrix","0"],["Cols","parameter","Int","Columns","Number of columns read","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful read","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously reads a matrix or part of it from the D3-Net network. The matrix of values is specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This reading takes place in the background. After a successful read the value is stored in an internal buffer and a logical 1 appears on output St. This output should be connected to the En input of the StoreLongData module, which makes the values from the internal buffer available for further processing.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NWFloat","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Writes a float value to the D3-Net network","formula":"Writes float value to D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Target station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Variable identifier","512"],["Val","parameter","Float","Value","Value being written","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful write","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously writes a variable of type float to the D3-Net network, specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This writing takes place in the background. After a successful write a logical 1 appears on output St.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NWFloatMtx","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Writes float values into a matrix in the D3-Net network","formula":"Writes float matrix to D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Target station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Matrix identifier","512"],["RO","parameter","Int","Row Offset","Row offset for reading in the matrix","0"],["CO","parameter","Int","Column Offset","Column offset for reading in the matrix","0"],["Val1","parameter","Float","Value1","Value of the 1st row and 1st column of the matrix","0"],["...","parameter","Float","...","Further values of the matrix","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful write","-"]],"notes":["The number of inputs of this module is user-configurable. The maximum permitted number of inputs (i.e. the product of the number of rows and columns) is 60.","The module continuously writes into a matrix or part of it on the D3-Net network. The matrix of values is specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This writing takes place in the background. After a successful write a logical 1 appears on output St.","When the Direct write of the read data option is enabled, the Val inputs are not shown. The module then writes the data read by the preceding D3NRFloatMtx module. Its St output should be connected to the En input of this D3NWFloatMtx module.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NWInt","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Writes an int value to the D3-Net network","formula":"Writes int value to D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Target station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Variable identifier","512"],["Val","parameter","Int","Value","Value being written","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful write","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously writes a variable of type int to the D3-Net network, specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This writing takes place in the background. After a successful write a logical 1 appears on output St.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NWIntMtx","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Writes int values into a matrix in the D3-Net network","formula":"Writes int matrix to D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Target station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Matrix identifier","512"],["RO","parameter","Int","Row Offset","Row offset for reading in the matrix","0"],["CO","parameter","Int","Column Offset","Column offset for reading in the matrix","0"],["Val1","parameter","Int","Value1","Value of the 1st row and 1st column of the matrix","0"],["...","parameter","Int","...","Further values of the matrix","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful write","-"]],"notes":["The number of inputs of this module is user-configurable. The maximum permitted number of inputs (i.e. the product of the number of rows and columns) is 120.","The module continuously writes into a matrix or part of it on the D3-Net network. The matrix of values is specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This writing takes place in the background. After a successful write a logical 1 appears on output St.","When the Direct write of the read data option is enabled, the Val inputs are not shown. The module then writes the data read by the preceding D3NRIntMtx module. Its St output should be connected to the En input of this D3NWIntMtx module.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NWLong","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Writes a long value to the D3-Net network","formula":"Writes long value to D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Target station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Variable identifier","512"],["Val","parameter","Long","Value","Value being written","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful write","-"]],"notes":["The module continuously writes a variable of type long to the D3-Net network, specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This writing takes place in the background. After a successful write a logical 1 appears on output St.","If the WID input is set to -1, the system time is written to the station specified by the Addr input.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"D3NWLongMtx","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Writes long values into a matrix in the D3-Net network","formula":"Writes long matrix to D3Net.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","Target station address in the D3-Net network","0"],["WID","parameter","Int","WID","Matrix identifier","512"],["RO","parameter","Int","Row Offset","Row offset for reading in the matrix","0"],["CO","parameter","Int","Column Offset","Column offset for reading in the matrix","0"],["Val1","parameter","Long","Value1","Value of the 1st row and 1st column of the matrix","0"],["...","parameter","Long","...","Further values of the matrix","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Set to logical 1 after a successful write","-"]],"notes":["The number of inputs of this module is user-configurable. The maximum permitted number of inputs (i.e. the product of the number of rows and columns) is 60.","The module continuously writes into a matrix or part of it on the D3-Net network. The matrix of values is specified by the station address Addr and the identifier WID. This writing takes place in the background. After a successful write a logical 1 appears on output St.","When the Direct write of the read data option is enabled, the Val inputs are not shown. The module then writes the data read by the preceding D3NRLongMtx module. Its St output should be connected to the En input of this D3NWLongMtx module.","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"StoreFloatData","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Exposes values from the internal buffer read by D3NRFloat or D3NRFloatMtx","formula":"Reads float data from internal buffer for D3Net communication.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Ofs","parameter","Int","Offset","Offset of value D0 in the internal buffer","0"],["D0","output","Float","Data0","Value of the internal buffer at offset Ofs","-"]],"notes":["The number of outputs of this module is user-configurable.","The float values read from the D3-Net network by the D3NRFloat or D3NRFloatMtx modules are stored in an internal buffer. To work further with these values the StoreFloatData module must be used; it copies the internal buffer starting at offset Ofs into outputs D0 to DN.","This module should come immediately after the D3NRFloat/D3NRFloatMtx reading module!","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"StoreIntData","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Exposes values from the internal buffer read by D3NRInt or D3NRIntMtx","formula":"Reads int data from internal buffer for D3Net communication.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Ofs","parameter","Int","Offset","Offset of value D0 in the internal buffer","0"],["D0","output","Int","Data0","Value of the internal buffer at offset Ofs","-"]],"notes":["The number of outputs of this module is user-configurable.","The int values read from the D3-Net network by the D3NRInt or D3NRIntMtx modules are stored in an internal buffer. To work further with these values the StoreIntData module must be used; it copies the internal buffer starting at offset Ofs into outputs D0 to DN.","This module should come immediately after the D3NRInt/D3NRIntMtx reading module!","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"StoreLongData","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Exposes values from the internal buffer read by D3NRLong or D3NRLongMtx","formula":"Reads long data from internal buffer for D3Net communication.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Ofs","parameter","Int","Offset","Offset of value D0 in the internal buffer","0"],["D0","output","Long","Data0","Value of the internal buffer at offset Ofs","-"]],"notes":["The number of outputs of this module is user-configurable.","The long values read from the D3-Net network by the D3NRLong or D3NRLongMtx modules are stored in an internal buffer. To work further with these values the StoreLongData module must be used; it copies the internal buffer starting at offset Ofs into outputs D0 to DN.","This module should come immediately after the D3NRLong/D3NRLongMtx reading module!","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"UserComm","category":"Communication","group":"","title":"Control of communication on the PLC user communication port","formula":"Starts communication on the second COM port","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["I1","input","Int","Input1","First input","0"],["Setup","parameter","Int","Setup","Setting of the communication parameters","0"],["RxLen","parameter","Int","RxLength","Number of bytes of the received message","0"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","Communication state, =1..reception OK",""]],"notes":["The number of inputs of this module is user-configurable.","This module sends the message given by the values on inputs Ix and then receives a message of length RxLen and stores it in an internal buffer. The communication takes place in the background. To make the received message available, StoreXxxData modules can be used with a special value on the Offset input.","The Setup input defines the communication parameters such as baud rate, parity and number of bits. The value on the Setup input is given by the sum of the BRG divider ratio and the FMT character format according to the following table:","The message to be sent is defined by the values on the inputs Ix. Special values on these inputs allow values to be converted to ASCII characters, a message checksum to be computed, and so on. The list of these values is given in the following table:","Codes 0x02..0x04 are used to send 16-bit values. The following inputs (their number is given by the LSB of the code) are treated as 16-bit values to be transmitted in the given manner. For example code 0x0302 converts the values of the following two inputs into ASCII form and sends them out through the communication port.","The received message bytes are stored in an internal buffer. One or more StoreXxxData modules are needed to make them available. The lower 8 bits of the Offset input give the start of the data in the buffer, while the upper 8 bits (MSB) determine the data conversion method according to the following table:","Thread no. 3 must always be used for this module!"],"tables":[{"head":["BRG","Baud (Baud)","","FMT","Formát znaku (Character format)"],"rows":[["0x01","115200","","0x000","8N1"],["0x02","57600","","0x500","8N2"],["0x03","38400","","0x300","8E1 (sudá parita)"],["0x06","19200","","0x700","8O1 (lichá parita)"],["0x0C","9600","","0x100","8S1 (par. bit = 0)"],["0x18","4800","","",""],["0x30","2400","","0x900","9N1 (9-bitová data)"],["0x60","1200","","",""],["0xC0","600","","",""]]},{"head":["MSB(InputX)","Popis (Description)","Poznámka (Note)"],"rows":[["0x00, 0x01","Zápis byte",""],["0x02","Zápis 16-bitových hodnot","LSB=počet"],["0x03","Zápis ASCII 16-bitových hodnot","LSB=počet"],["0x04","Zápis 16-bitových hodnot Big-Endian","LSB=počet"],["0x06","Zápis skupiny opakujících se 8-bitových hodnot","LSB=počet"],["0x07","Zápis skupiny opakujících se 16-bitových hodnot","LSB=počet"],["0x0A","Zápis 8-bitové ASCII hodnoty z LSB",""],["0x0B","Zápis 8-bitové ASCII sumy předchozích ASCII znaků",""],["0x0C","Zápis byte sumy předchozích bajtů","LSB=počet"],["0x0D","Zápis ASCII sumy předchozích bajtů","LSB=počet"],["0x0E","Zápis xor předchozích bajtů","LSB=počet"],["0x0F","Zápis ASCII xor předchozích bajtů","LSB=počet"],["0x16","Zápis CRC16 předchozích bajtů, init=FFFF","LSB=počet"],["0x17","Zápis CRC16 předchozích bajtů, init=0000","LSB=počet"]]},{"head":["MSB(Offset)","Popis (Description)","Poznámka (Note)"],"rows":[["0x01","Čtení samostatných bajtů","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x02","Čtení Int/Long/Float hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x03","Čtení ASCII 16-bitových hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x04","Čtení 16-bitových hodnot Big-Endian","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x0A","Čtení ASCII 8-bitových hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x11","Čtení 8-bitových BCD hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x12","Čtení 16-bitových BCD hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x13","Čtení 24-bitových BCD hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x14","Čtení 32-bitových BCD hodnot","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x21","Čtení 8-bitových BCD hodnot se znaménkem","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x22","Čtení 16-bitových BCD hodnot se znaménkem","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x23","Čtení 24-bitových BCD hodnot se znaménkem","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x24","Čtení 32-bitových BCD hodnot se znaménkem","LSB = od kterého znaku"],["0x0B","Čtení 8-bitové sumy předchozích ASCII znaků","Výpočet sumy/xor/CRC16:LSB[0..3] ... od kterého znakuLSB[4..7] ... bez kolika znaků od konce"],["0x0C","Čtení 8-bitové sumy předchozích bajtů",""],["0x0E","Čtení 8-bitové xor předchozích bajtů",""],["0x0F","Čtení 8-bitové xor předchozích ASCII znaků",""],["0x16","Čtení CRC16 init=FFFF",""],["0x17","Čtení CRC16 init=0000",""]]}]},{"name":"Macro","category":"Macro","group":"","title":"Execution of a macro","formula":"Macro Block","pins":[],"notes":["The list of the macro's inputs and outputs depends on its definition.","The module is used to execute a macro defined on the corresponding sheet of the project. Inserting a macro block into the program has the same effect as inserting all blocks of that macro and wiring them to the corresponding signals.","To create a macro definition a new sheet must be created whose name starts with the * character; for example a sheet named *Makro defines a macro named Makro.","The macro sheet contains the Macro IO blocks that define the macro interface together with the other functional blocks of the macro. Depending on the interface definition, a given macro can have a different number, names and data types of pins. The figure above shows an example of a macro with one input, one parameter and one output pin of type Bit."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Macro IO","category":"Macro","group":"","title":"Definition of a macro's inputs, parameters and outputs","formula":"Macro Interface","pins":[["Inp1","input","Bit","Vstup 1","Macro input pin","0"],["Par1","input","Bit","Parametr 1","Macro parameter","0"],["Out1","output","Bit","Výstup 1","Macro output pin",""]],"notes":["The module defines the macro interface - the macro's inputs, parameters and outputs. This module must be inserted into the macro page three times in sequence: first as the input definition block (Inputs), then as the parameter definition block (Params) and finally as the macro output definition block (Outputs).","The number, names and data types of the pins of these blocks are defined in the module configuration dialog.","The New pin and Delete pin buttons add or remove macro pins. Clicking a pin name in the table renames it. The data type of the selected pin is set with the buttons in the Pin type group. The order of the pins can be changed by dragging a row with the mouse.","If a macro has no inputs, parameters or outputs, the corresponding module can be deleted from the macro sheet, or all pins can be deleted in its configuration."],"tables":[]},{"name":"CreateIntArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Allocates memory for an Int array","formula":"Allocates memory for an integer array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Len","input","Long","Length","Array length - number of elements of type Int","16"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","1 if the operation succeeded, otherwise 0","-"]],"notes":["The module allocates memory for the array given by the Id input. The number of array elements is given by the value of the Len input. Output St is set to 1 if the array was created successfully. If there is not enough free memory for the operation, or if the array Id is outside the permitted range, output St is set to 0.","If an array with the same length has already been created previously, no action is taken and output St is set to 1. Otherwise any previously allocated array is released and the newly allocated array contains the value 0 in all cells.","The range of the array identifier Id depends on the module firmware. At present, values of Id from 0 to 15 are supported on PIC32-series units."],"tables":[]},{"name":"CreateLongArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Allocates memory for a Long or Float array","formula":"Allocates memory for an long or float array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Len","input","Long","Length","Array length - number of elements of type Long or Float","16"],["St","output","Boolean","Status","1 if the operation succeeded, otherwise 0","-"]],"notes":["The module allocates memory for the array given by the Id input. The number of array elements is given by the value of the Len input. Output St is set to 1 if the array was created successfully. If there is not enough free memory for the operation, or if the array Id is outside the permitted range, output St is set to 0.","If an array with the same length has already been created previously, no action is taken and output St is set to 1. Otherwise any previously allocated array is released and the newly allocated array contains the value 0 in all cells.","The range of the array identifier Id depends on the module firmware. At present, values of Id from 0 to 15 are supported on PIC32-series units."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ReadFloatArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Reads the value of one element of a Float array","formula":"Reads an element from an float array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Idx","input","Long","Index","Index in the array, in the range 0 - (array length - 1)","0"],["Y","output","Float","Výstup","Value of the array element","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the value of the array element number Index of the array given by the Id input and writes the result to the module output.","If the array Id or the Index is outside the permitted range, the value 0 is written to the module output."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ReadIntArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Reads the value of one element of an Int array","formula":"Reads an element from an integer array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Idx","input","Long","Index","Index in the array, in the range 0 - (array length - 1)","0"],["Y","output","Int","Výstup","Value of the array element","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the value of the array element number Index of the array given by the Id input and writes the result to the module output.","If the array Id or the Index is outside the permitted range, the value 0 is written to the module output."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ReadLongArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Reads the value of one element of a Long array","formula":"Reads an element from an long array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Idx","input","Long","Index","Index in the array, in the range 0 - (array length - 1)","0"],["Y","output","Long","Výstup","Value of the array element","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the value of the array element number Index of the array given by the Id input and writes the result to the module output.","If the array Id or the Index is outside the permitted range, the value 0 is written to the module output."],"tables":[]},{"name":"WriteFloatArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Writes the value of one element of a Float array","formula":"Writes value to an float array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Idx","input","Long","Index","Index in the array, in the range 0 - (array length - 1)","0"],["X","input","Float","Hodnota","Value to be written",""],["Y","output","Float","Výstup","Value of the array element","-"]],"notes":["The module writes the value from input X into the array element number Index of the array given by the Id input and writes the same value to the module output.","If the array Id or the Index is outside the permitted range, the array element is not written and the value of output Y remains unchanged."],"tables":[]},{"name":"WriteIntArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Writes the value of one element of an Int array","formula":"Writes value to an integer array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Idx","input","Long","Index","Index in the array, in the range 0 - (array length - 1)","0"],["X","input","Int","Hodnota","Value to be written",""],["Y","output","Int","Výstup","Value of the array element","-"]],"notes":["The module writes the value from input X into the array element number Index of the array given by the Id input and writes the same value to the module output.","If the array Id or the Index is outside the permitted range, the array element is not written and the value of output Y remains unchanged."],"tables":[]},{"name":"WriteLongArray","category":"Main","group":"Arrays","title":"Writes the value of one element of a Long array","formula":"Writes value to an long array","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Id","input","Int","Id","Array identifier","0"],["Idx","input","Long","Index","Index in the array, in the range 0 - (array length - 1)","0"],["X","input","Long","Hodnota","Value to be written",""],["Y","output","Long","Výstup","Value of the array element","-"]],"notes":["The module writes the value from input X into the array element number Index of the array given by the Id input and writes the same value to the module output.","If the array Id or the Index is outside the permitted range, the array element is not written and the value of output Y remains unchanged."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Comparator","category":"Main","group":"Comparators","title":"Compares int values","formula":"Compares values A and B","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["A","input","Int","A","Value A","0"],["B","input","Int","B","Value B","0"],["AGtB","output","Boolean","A greater than B","1 if A>B, otherwise 0","-"],["AEqB","output","Boolean","A equal B","1 if A=B, otherwise 0","-"],["ALtB","output","Boolean","A less than B","1 if A<B, otherwise 0","-"]],"notes":["The module compares the input values A and B and, according to their values, sets exactly one of the outputs to 1. The remaining two outputs are cleared."],"tables":[]},{"name":"HystComparator","category":"Main","group":"Comparators","title":"Compares int values with hysteresis","formula":"Compares values A and B with hysteresis","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["A","input","Int","A","Value A","0"],["B","input","Int","B","Value B","0"],["HalfHyst","parameter","Int","Half hysteresis","Hysteresis half-width","0"],["AGtB","output","Boolean","A greater than B","Display of the A>B state","-"],["AEqB","output","Boolean","A equal B","Display of the A=B state","-"],["ALtB","output","Boolean","A less than B","Display of the A<B state","-"]],"notes":["The module works similarly to Comparator, except that it compares the input values A and B with a configured hysteresis. Output AGtB is set when A>(B+HalfHyst) and cleared when A<(B-HalfHyst). Similarly output ALtB is set by the condition A<(B-HalfHyst) and cleared by A>(B+HalfHyst). The value of output AEqB corresponds to the condition A>=(B-HalfHyst) and at the same time A<=(B+HalfHyst)."],"tables":[]},{"name":"InRange","category":"Main","group":"Comparators","title":"Determines whether a value lies within a given interval","formula":"Returns 1 if X is between L and H","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Long","X","Input value","0"],["L","parameter","Int","Low","Lower interval limit","0"],["H","parameter","Int","High","Upper interval limit","0"],["Y","output","Boolean","Y","Output value","-"]],"notes":["InRange compares the value of input X with the given interval limits. When L<=H the value of output Y equals the condition (X>=L) and at the same time (X<H), i.e. X lies between L (inclusive) and H. If L>H the output value corresponds to the condition (X<L) or (X>=H).","This approach allows the module to be used, for example, as a time switch where the hours are fed to input X. The parameter L then gives the switch-on time and H the switch-off time, with the transition across midnight also handled."],"tables":[]},{"name":"LComparator","category":"Main","group":"Comparators","title":"Compares Long values","formula":"Compares values A and B","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["A","input","Long","A","Value A","0"],["B","input","Long","B","Value B","0"],["AGtB","output","Boolean","A greater than B","1 if A>B, otherwise 0","-"],["AEqB","output","Boolean","A equal B","1 if A=B, otherwise 0","-"],["ALtB","output","Boolean","A less than B","1 if A<B, otherwise 0","-"]],"notes":["The module compares the input values A and B and, according to their values, sets exactly one of the outputs to 1. The remaining two outputs are cleared."],"tables":[]},{"name":"MCompare","category":"Main","group":"Comparators","title":"Comparison of the input value against several Long values","formula":"Compares values X with values C1..Cn","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Long","Input","Input value","0"],["C1 - Cn","parameters","Long","C1 - Cn","Value inputs","0"],["N","output","Int","Index","Output","-"]],"notes":["The module searches for the value on input X among the constants on inputs C1-Cn and returns the ordinal number of the first constant equal to the value on input X. If no match is found, output N is cleared.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 16."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Bits2Int","category":"Main","group":"Conversion","title":"Composes an int value from 16 binary inputs","formula":"Converts bits to int","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["B0","input","Boolean","Bit 0","Input value of bit order 0","0"],["B1","input","Boolean","Bit 1","Input value of bit order 1","0"],["B2","input","Boolean","Bit 2","Input value of bit order 2","0"],["B3","input","Boolean","Bit 3","Input value of bit order 3","0"],["B4","input","Boolean","Bit 4","Input value of bit order 4","0"],["B5","input","Boolean","Bit 5","Input value of bit order 5","0"],["B6","input","Boolean","Bit 6","Input value of bit order 6","0"],["B7","input","Boolean","Bit 7","Input value of bit order 7","0"],["B8","input","Boolean","Bit 8","Input value of bit order 8","0"],["B9","input","Boolean","Bit 9","Input value of bit order 9","0"],["B10","input","Boolean","Bit 10","Input value of bit order 10","0"],["B11","input","Boolean","Bit 11","Input value of bit order 11","0"],["B12","input","Boolean","Bit 12","Input value of bit order 12","0"],["B13","input","Boolean","Bit 13","Input value of bit order 13","0"],["B14","input","Boolean","Bit 14","Input value of bit order 14","0"],["B15","input","Boolean","Bit 15","Input value of bit order 15","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Output value","-"]],"notes":["The resulting value of output Y is composed of the individual input bits. Each input B0 to B15 represents the corresponding binary digit place. Y=B0.2^0 +B1.2^1 +...+B15.2^15"],"tables":[]},{"name":"Int2Bits","category":"Main","group":"Conversion","title":"Exposes the individual bits of an int value","formula":"Expands int into bits","pins":[["X","input","Int","X","Input value","0"],["B0","output","Boolean","Bit 0","Lowest bit of value X","-"],["B15","output","Boolean","Bit 15","Highest bit of value X","-"]],"notes":["The module exposes the individual bits of the value on input X."],"tables":[]},{"name":"If","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"Conditional execution of the program","formula":"Conditional Execution","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Enables execution of the modules following this If module","1"]],"notes":["The If module, together with the Else and EndIf modules, is used for conditional execution of a part of the program. The modules lying between the If module and Else or EndIf are executed when the En input has the value 1. The modules between the optional Else module and EndIf are executed when the En input has the value 0.","The En input of the If module can be inverted (the \"If not\" function).","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Else","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"Second part of the If program construct","formula":"Conditional Execution","pins":[],"notes":["The Else module, together with the If and EndIf modules, is used for conditional execution of a part of the program. The modules lying between the Else module and EndIf are executed when the En input of the preceding If module has the value 0.","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"EndIf","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"End of the If program construct","formula":"Conditional Execution","pins":[],"notes":["The EndIf module terminates the conditionally executed part of the program started by an If block.","This module may contain one or more user-defined outputs. Their values can be set by Results modules placed in the individual parts of the If construct.","The number, names and data types of the pins are defined in the module configuration dialog.","The New pin and Delete pin buttons add or remove the module's output pins. Clicking a pin name in the table renames it. The data type of the selected pin is set with the buttons in the Pin type group. The order of the pins can be changed by dragging a row with the mouse.","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Switch","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"Execution of a part of the program depending on the value of the input","formula":"","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Enables execution of the whole Switch - EndSwitch sequence","1"],["Sw","input","Int","Switch","Control input","1"]],"notes":["The Switch module, together with the Case, Default and EndSwitch modules, is used for conditional execution of a part of the program. According to the numeric value on input Sw, the part of the program starting at the Case module with the matching value is executed. If the value of Sw matches no Case module, the part of the program following the Default module is executed (if one is used). The whole sequence is terminated by the EndSwitch module.","The En input of the Switch module can be inverted. If there is a logical 0 on this input, all following modules up to the EndSwitch module are skipped.","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Case","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"Label of the Switch construct","formula":"","pins":[],"notes":["The Case module is part of the Switch - Case - Default - EndSwitch program construct. It marks the part of the program that is executed when the value of the Sw input of the Switch module matches the value (or one of the values) of this Case module.","In the Case module configuration window one or more values, or ranges of consecutive values, can be defined. Individual values are separated by commas; a range of values is defined as start..end value.","For example, the entry 1, 5..7, 9 defines the values 1, 5, 6, 7, 9.","The values of the individual Case modules within a single Switch - EndSwitch construct must not repeat, i.e. two Case modules must not contain the same value.","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Default","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"Default label of the Switch construct","formula":"Conditional Execution","pins":[],"notes":["The Default module is part of the Switch - Case - Default - EndSwitch program construct. It marks the part of the program that is executed when the value of the Sw input of the Switch module matches no Case module.","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"EndSwitch","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"End of the Switch program construct","formula":"Set switch results","pins":[],"notes":["The EndSwitch module terminates the conditionally executed part of the program started by a Switch block.","This module may contain one or more user-defined outputs. Their values can be set by Results modules placed in the individual parts of the Switch construct.","The number, names and data types of the pins are defined in the module configuration dialog.","The New pin and Delete pin buttons add or remove the module's output pins. Clicking a pin name in the table renames it. The data type of the selected pin is set with the buttons in the Pin type group. The order of the pins can be changed by dragging a row with the mouse.","Which modules are affected by the conditional execution is determined by their order (O:xxx) within the thread."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Results","category":"Main","group":"Execution","title":"Writes results to the outputs of the terminating EndIf / EndSwitch block","formula":"Set switch results","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Vstup1","input","Bit/Int/Long/Float","volitelný","Input value","0"],["Vstup2","input","Bit/Int/Long/Float","volitelný","Input value","0"]],"notes":["The module writes the values from its inputs to the identically named outputs of the nearest corresponding EndIf or EndSwitch module. It is used inside an If / EndIf or Switch / EndSwitch construct to write the resulting values for a given state.","The number, names and data types of the pins are defined in the module configuration dialog.","The New pin and Delete pin buttons add or remove the module's input pins. Clicking a pin name in the table renames it. The data type of the selected pin is set with the buttons in the Pin type group. The order of the pins can be changed by dragging a row with the mouse."],"tables":[]},{"name":"CalibTransf","category":"Main","group":"Filters","title":"Three-point linear transformation of an int value","formula":"Transfer X calibrated on XMin-XCenter-XMax to Y in range YMin-YCenter-YMax.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Int","X","Input value","0"],["XMax","parameter","Int","Maximum X","Maximum value of input X","0"],["XMid","parameter","Int","Middle X","Mean value of input X","0"],["XMin","parameter","Int","Minimum X","Minimum value of input X","0"],["YMax","parameter","Int","Maximum Y","Maximum value of output Y","0"],["YMid","parameter","Int","Middle Y","Mean value of output Y","0"],["YMin","parameter","Int","Minimum Y","Minimum value of output Y","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Output value","-"]],"notes":["The parameters XMin, XMid and XMax divide the range of input X into 4 intervals. If X<=XMin, output Y takes the value YMin; similarly when X>=XMax, output Y takes the value YMax. Input values in the interval XMin to XMid map to a proportional output value between YMin and YMid, and analogously input values in the interval XMid to XMax map to a proportional output value between YMid and YMax.","The values on inputs Xmax to Xmin must be sorted from the highest to the lowest.","The graphical representation is shown in the following figure.","The number of calibration points of this module is user-configurable in the range 2 - 17."],"tables":[]},{"name":"DelayFilter","category":"Main","group":"Filters","title":"Filters short pulses of a binary value","formula":"Input signal must persist for specified cycles (Delay) to appear on output","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["In","input","Boolean","Input","Input signal","0"],["Dly","parameter","Int","Delay","Delay length","0"],["Cnt","output","Int","Counter","Countdown of the remaining cycles","-"],["Out","output","Boolean","Output","Output signal","-"]],"notes":["If a logical 1 appears on input In, the module starts counting the passes through the process cycle in which it is processed. The initial countdown value Cnt equals the size of the parameter Dly and is decremented by 1 with each cycle while the input is active (=1). After counting down to 0, a logical 1 is set on output Out. Whenever input In is cleared, output Out is also cleared and Cnt is set to the value of the parameter Dly.","For example, if you want to filter out pulses shorter than 5 s, place the module in the \"Timer 1s\" process and set the Dly parameter to 5. The pulses that pass through to output Out will be shortened by 5 s."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Filter","category":"Main","group":"Filters","title":"Filter implementing a 1st-order time delay","formula":"First-order filter","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Int","Input","Input value to be filtered","0"],["T","parameter","Int","Time","Filter time constant","10"],["Y","output","Int","Output","Filtered value","-"]],"notes":["Input value to be filtered","The module filters input X. The filter delay (the time in which the output reaches about 63% of the input value) is given by the parameter T."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ILimiter","category":"Main","group":"Filters","title":"Limits the value to the given interval","formula":"Value is limited in range Min..Max","pins":[["X","input","Long","X","Input value","0"],["Max","parameter","Int","Max","Maximum permitted output value","0"],["Min","parameter","Int","Min","Minimum permitted output value","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Limited value","-"]],"notes":["The module limits the value of input X to the interval given by the parameters Min and Max. If X < Min, output Y takes the value Min; similarly if X > Max, output Y takes the value Max. The input value X has the extended Long data type range."],"tables":[]},{"name":"LLimiter","category":"Main","group":"Filters","title":"Limits the value to the given interval","formula":"Value is limited in range Min..Max","pins":[["X","input","Long","X","Input value","0"],["Max","parameter","Long","Max","Maximum permitted output value","0"],["Min","parameter","Long","Min","Minimum permitted output value","0"],["Y","output","Long","Y","Limited value","-"]],"notes":["The module limits the value of input X to the interval given by the parameters Min and Max. If X < Min, output Y takes the value Min; similarly if X > Max, output Y takes the value Max."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Ramp","category":"Main","group":"Filters","title":"Creates a ramp for a stepwise-changing value","formula":"Ramped value move","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Int","X","Input value","0"],["SU","parameter","Int","Step up","Maximum change of the output value upwards","0"],["SD","parameter","Int","Step down","Maximum change of the output value downwards","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Output value","-"]],"notes":["If the value on input X differs from the value on output Y, the module tries to bring Y closer to X. In each cycle, however, Y is increased by at most the value of the SU parameter, or decreased by at most the value of the SD parameter. A step change of input X therefore results in a smooth change of output Y along a ramp whose upward slope is given by SU and downward slope by SD."],"tables":[]},{"name":"AdvCounter","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Event counter with range limiting and preset","formula":"Increases Y by Step on Trigger 0->1 event","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Tr","input","Boolean","Trigger","On a transition from 0 to 1, St is added to output Y","0"],["Rst","input","Boolean","Reset","If active (=1), output Y is cleared","0"],["Pres","input","Boolean","Preset","If active (=1), output Y is set to the value PV","0"],["EnH","input","Boolean","EnableH","If active (=1), output Y is limited from above by the value Max","0"],["EnL","input","Boolean","EnableL","If active (=1), output Y is limited from below by the value Min","0"],["PV","parameter","Int","PresetVal","Preset counter value. Activated by the Preset input.","0"],["Max","parameter","Int","Maximum","Upper counter limit","0"],["Min","parameter","Int","Minimum","Lower counter limit","0"],["St","parameter","Int","Step","Size of the step by which the value of output Y is increased","1"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Counter state","-"],["H","output","Boolean","High","Indicates that the value Max has been reached. Set when Y >= Max.","-"],["L","output","Boolean","Low","Indicates that the value Min has been reached. Set when Y <= Min.","-"]],"notes":["The module monitors the state of input Tr. On a rising edge (transition from 0 to 1) it increases the value of output Y by the value of the parameter St.","If the Rst input is active, the value of output Y is cleared.","If the Preset input is active, the value of output Y is set to the value of the PV parameter.","If the EnH or EnL input is active, the value of output Y is limited from above by the Max parameter or from below by the Min parameter respectively.","Outputs H and L respectively are set when the value of output Y reaches the limit given by the Max or Min parameter. These outputs work independently of whether output limiting is enabled by the EnH and EnL inputs."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Copy","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Copy of values","formula":"Y = X","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X0","input","Bit/Int/Long/Float","X0","Input value","0"],["Y0","output","Bit/Int/Long/Float","Y0","Output value","-"]],"notes":["The module copies one or more values from inputs Xn to outputs Yn. The data type of the inputs and outputs is set automatically at compile time according to the values connected to the Xn inputs.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 100."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Counter","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Event counter","formula":"Increases Y by Step on Trigger 0->1 event","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Tr","input","Boolean","Trigger","On a transition from 0 to 1, St is added to output Y","0"],["Rst","input","Boolean","Reset","If active (=1), output Y is cleared","0"],["St","parameter","Int","Step","Size of the step by which the value of output Y is increased","1"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Counter state","-"]],"notes":["The module monitors the state of input Tr. On a rising edge (transition from 0 to 1) it increases the value of output Y by the value of the parameter St. If the Rst input is active, the value of output Y is cleared."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Logger","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Records data into the archive memory","formula":"Writes data log into archive memory","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["I1 - In","input","Int","Ints","Inputs of type Int","0"],["L1 - Ln","input","Long","Longs","Inputs of type Long","0"],["F1 - Fn","input","Float","Floats","Inputs of type Float","1"],["Idx","output","Int","Index","Index (archive row number) for the next write","-"]],"notes":["Logger writes the values of the signals on inputs Ix, Lx and Fx into the PLC archive memory so that they can be read out later by a PC. The write takes place in every cycle in which the En input has the value 1. Besides the input signal values, each record also contains the PLC system time.","In the configuration dialog the number of Int, Long and Float inputs, the archive length and the start address in the archive memory can be chosen. Below these values the size of one archive row (Row size), the total archive length and the next free address in the archive memory are shown. In order to minimise the time needed to write a row into the archive memory it is advisable for the row size to be a power of 2 (8, 16, 32, 64, 128 B).","In the lower part of the dialog there is a signal table showing the wiring of the module's individual inputs. For each input the name of the column in the table into which the PC archive will write can be entered. When a DBase-type table is used the field name length is limited to 10 characters.","The following example shows the use of the Logger module to archive 4 signals every 10 seconds. The Trigger block sets output Y to 1 on every change of the tens-of-seconds value (seconds / 10). The Index output of the Logger module is fed to the input of the SaveData module. This ensures that after a power failure or other PLC reset the archive write continues at the next free row."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Move","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Copies an int value","formula":"Moves value X to Y when triggered","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Tr","input","Boolean","Trigger","On a transition from 0 to 1, the value of input X is stored to output Y","0"],["X","input","Int","X","Input value","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Last requested copy of input X","-"]],"notes":["The module monitors the state of input Tr. On a rising edge (transition from 0 to 1) it copies the value of input X to output Y."],"tables":[]},{"name":"P3Menu","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Editor of the PLC Sybas P3 menu","formula":"Menu designer","pins":[],"notes":["The module has no inputs or outputs. It only serves to configure the menu via its configuration dialog","The left part of the configuration window shows the menu structure. The Add item button adds a new item to the menu; Add submenu also creates a new item but places it in the submenu of the selected item. The Move up and Move down buttons move the selected item within its level. The last button, Delete item, deletes the selected item. The right part of the window is used to set the properties of the selected item. The Text field contains the text that will be displayed on the top line of the display. The bottom line can show the value of a variable (or parameter) which you assign to the Value field. The remaining fields and options relate to the display of that value. The Read only option prevents the variable from being edited. Checking Use 1/K means that instead of the value K (explained below) its reciprocal value is used. The Change Q option means that after editing the variable value using the PLC buttons, the variable/parameter given by the Value field will not be changed; instead the value of the variable/parameter Q is changed so that the displayed value corresponds to the value set by the edit. The Min and Max fields define the editing range of the variable/parameter. The values K and Q perform the linear transformation Y=K.X+Q between the displayed value (Y) and the variable/parameter (X). A direct value (within the permitted range) can be entered into the K and Q fields, or they can be connected to variables/parameters (in which case the Change Q option is meaningful). The last field, Decimals, determines the number of decimal places shown on the display.","The # character controls the position and formatting of the displayed value. By default the value is shown on the second line of the display, aligned fully to the right. If additional text is to be displayed after the value (e.g. a unit), the # character is used in place of the last digit of the displayed value. For example the text \"Tepl. dílna #°C\" displays the unit °C after the temperature.","If a certain minimum number of digits is to be displayed (leading zeros), that area is marked with the @ characters, e.g. \"Venkovní tepl. @@@#°C\".","The value can also be displayed in hexadecimal or binary notation using the character pair X# or B#. When editing two-state values (0/1), the following texts can be displayed instead of the numeric value:","0# OFF/ON 1# OFF/ON 2# NO/YES 3# FAULT/OK","This module may be used only once in a project!"],"tables":[]},{"name":"SaveData","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Stores/restores data to/from FRAM","formula":"Stores/restores data into/from FRAM","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["I1","input","Long","I1","Stored value","0"],["Addr","parameter","Int","Address","FRAM address","0"]],"notes":["The number of inputs of this module is user-configurable.","In the 1st cycle of the process SaveData reads the values stored in FRAM from address Addr and places them into the variables connected to inputs I1 to IN. In subsequent cycles the values of those variables are instead stored into FRAM at the corresponding addresses."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Set","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Sets the variables connected to inputs P1-Pn to the value of input X","formula":"Set values of the pin X to the pins P1..Pn","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Long","Input","Input value","0"],["P1 - Pn","input","Long","P1 - Pn","Pins being set","0"]],"notes":["If the En input = 1, the value from input X is written into the variables (outputs of other modules) connected to inputs P1-Pn.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 126."],"tables":[]},{"name":"SetIdx","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Sets the selected variable connected to inputs P0-Pn-1 to the value of input X","formula":"Set values of the pin X to the pin P[Idx]","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Idx","input","Int","Index","Index - number of the input P being written","0"],["X","input","Long","Input","Input value","0"],["P0 - Pn-1","input","Long","P0 - Pn-1","Pins being set","0"]],"notes":["If the En input = 1, the value from input X is written into the variable (output of another module) connected to input Pidx. The value of input Idx must be in the range 0 to N-1, otherwise no write takes place.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 126."],"tables":[]},{"name":"SystemCmd","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Performs a system command","formula":"Performs firmware-specific system command.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0"],["Par1","input","Int","Parametr1","First parameter","0"],["Par1","input","Int","Parametr2","Second parameter","0"],["Out","output","Int","Output","Output value","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0000"],["FW","output","Int","Output","Output value","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0001"],["Tmr","output","Int","Output","Output value","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0004"],["Par1","input","Int","Parametr1","Not used","0"],["Tmr","output","Int","Output","Output value","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x000F"],["DoNum","input","Int","DO Number","Output number 0 - 23","0"],["Current","output","Int","Output","Output current value","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0010"],["Zr_U","input","Int","Zero U","Voltage limit (630 = 1 V)","0"],["Zr_I","input","Int","Zero I","Current limit (x 0.5 mA)","0"],["Out","output","Int","Output","Not used","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0020"],["BitNr","input","Int","Bit Number","Ordinal number of the bit being searched for","0"],["Inp","input","Long","Input","Input value","0"],["BitPos","output","Int","Bit Position","Position of the bit found","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0100"],["Adr","output","Int","Adresa","Address of the module on the D3Net network","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0101"],["Addr","input","Int","Address","Requested address","0"],["Lock","input","Int","Lock","Lock of the RowNet address","0"],["Adr","output","Int","Output","Address on the RowNet network","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0102"],["Dir","output","Bit","Output","Direction of the RowNet network (0 = left to right, 1 = right to left)","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0103"],["BkTmr","output","Int","Output","Output value","-"],["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Cmd","input","Int","Command","Code of the requested function","0x0104"],["Addr","input","Int","Address","Unit address","0"],["Count","input","Int","Count","Number of units","0"],["Out","output","Int","Output","Returns the value of the Addr input","-"]],"notes":["The SystemCmd module performs the function given by the code on the Cmd input. The list of available functions depends on the device type.","Function 0x0000 returns the firmware type on output Fw.","Function 0x0000 returns the current firmware version on output Ver.","Function 0x0004 returns the current value of the system timer on output Tmr. On the P24 module the increment frequency is 1 kHz.","Function 0x0004 on the P24 module is used to verify that a load is connected to the output given by DoNum (0 - 23). The selected output is switched on briefly and the current flowing through the load connected to that output is measured. The resulting average current over that period is written to output Current.","Function 0x0010 on the P24 module sets the limits for monitoring zero voltage and zero current on switched-off digital outputs. If a voltage or current higher than the set limit appears on a switched-off output, that output is flagged with a zero-voltage or zero-current error. The number of the first switched-off output with a non-zero voltage can be obtained with the ReadAI module using channel number 200. Similarly, the number of the first switched-off output with a non-zero current can be obtained with ReadAI using channel number 201.","Function 0x0020 searches from the right for the position of the first non-zero bit in the word on input Inp. If no bit has the value 1 the result is 0, otherwise the number of the first non-zero bit from the right (range 1 - 32) is written to output BitPos. The BitNr input selects which non-zero bit is searched for: 1 = first non-zero bit, 2 = second non-zero bit, etc. If BitNr = 0 the output returns the upper 16 bits of the value Imp.","Function 0x0100 returns the current address of the module on the D3Net network, usually in the range 0 - 31.","Function 0x0101 allows the RowNet network address of the module to be read or set, and the lock mode of that address to be configured. If input Address > 0 and the program is executing its first cycle, the RowNet address is set to the value of the Address input. The Lock input sets the address lock mode: 0 = automatic unit numbering, 1 = automatic numbering upwards only (when a unit is added, so that addresses cannot be duplicated), 2 = full address lock.","Function 0x0102 returns the current direction of the RowNet network. 0 means unit numbering from left to right, 1 means the opposite direction","Function 0x0103 allows the delay between the cycles of the program's communication thread to be shortened. If the thread is currently in the delay between individual thread cycles, executing this function terminates the delay early and the thread starts immediately. Output BkTmr gives the amount by which the delay was shortened.","Function 0x0104 allows the address and unit count to be set for a read or write by the following DbnXxxx block. If the following communication block has the high byte of its address = 0x7F, the value of the Addr input of this block is used as the target unit address (adding 0x100 to Addr addresses all units from the current one up to the target). If the following communication block has the high byte of its address = 0x7E, the value of the Addr input is used as the target unit address and the value of the Count input as the number of units."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Trigger","category":"Main","group":"Other","title":"Monitors changes of a variable/parameter value","formula":"Generates binary impulse whenever X is changed","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["X","input","Int","X","Monitored value","0"],["Y","output","Boolean","Y","Change flag","-"]],"notes":["The module monitors the value connected to input X and sets output Y to logical 1 on every change of that value. If the value is the same as in the previous process cycle, output Y is cleared."],"tables":[]},{"name":"FDemux","category":"Main","group":"Switches","title":"Writes a Float value to the selected output Yidx","formula":"Compares values A and B with hysteresis","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Idx","input","Int","Index","Selector","0"],["X","input","Float","X","Value input","0"],["Y0 - Yn-1","output","Float","Out","Outputs","-"]],"notes":["The module sets the selected output Yidx to the value from input X. If Idx=0 the value X is copied to output Y0; if Idx=1 the value X is copied to output Y1, and so on. If the Idx input is outside the range 0 to (N-1) no write is performed. The values of the other Y outputs remain unchanged.","The number of outputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 126."],"tables":[]},{"name":"FSwitch","category":"Main","group":"Switches","title":"Selector between Float values","formula":"Switches between values of float data type, depending on switch state","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Sw","input","Int","Switch","Selector","0"],["X0 - Xn","input","Float","X0 - Xn","Value inputs","0"],["Y","output","Float","Out","Output","-"]],"notes":["The module sets output Y depending on the state of the selector Sw. If Sw=0 the value X0 is copied to output Y; if Sw=1 the value X1 is copied to output Y, and so on. If the Sw input is outside the range 0 to (N-1), output Y is cleared.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 16."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IDemux","category":"Main","group":"Switches","title":"Writes an Int value to the selected output Yidx","formula":"Compares values A and B with hysteresis","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Idx","input","Int","Index","Selector","0"],["X","input","Int","X","Value input","0"],["Y0 - Yn-1","output","Int","Out","Outputs","-"]],"notes":["The module sets the selected output Yidx to the value from input X. If Idx=0 the value X is copied to output Y0; if Idx=1 the value X is copied to output Y1, and so on. If the Idx input is outside the range 0 to (N-1) no write is performed. The values of the other Y outputs remain unchanged.","The number of outputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 126."],"tables":[]},{"name":"ISwitch","category":"Main","group":"Switches","title":"Selector between Int values","formula":"Switches between values of int data type, depending on switch state","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Sw","input","Int","Switch","Selector","0"],["X0 - Xn","input","Int","X0 - Xn","Value inputs","0"],["Y","output","Int","Out","Output","-"]],"notes":["The module sets output Y depending on the state of the selector Sw. If Sw=0 the value X0 is copied to output Y; if Sw=1 the value X1 is copied to output Y, and so on. If the Sw input is outside the range 0 to (N-1), output Y is cleared.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 16."],"tables":[]},{"name":"LDemux","category":"Main","group":"Switches","title":"Writes a Long value to the selected output Yidx","formula":"Set output Y[Idx] to the value of the pin X","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Idx","input","Int","Index","Selector","0"],["X","input","Long","X","Value input","0"],["Y0 - Yn-1","output","Long","Out","Outputs","-"]],"notes":["The module sets the selected output Yidx to the value from input X. If Idx=0 the value X is copied to output Y0; if Idx=1 the value X is copied to output Y1, and so on. If the Idx input is outside the range 0 to (N-1) no write is performed. The values of the other Y outputs remain unchanged.","The number of outputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 126."],"tables":[]},{"name":"LSwitch","category":"Main","group":"Switches","title":"Selector between Long values","formula":"Switches between values of long data type, depending on switch state","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Sw","input","Int","Switch","Selector","0"],["X0 - Xn","input","Long","X0 - Xn","Value inputs","0"],["Y","output","Long","Out","Output","-"]],"notes":["The module sets output Y depending on the state of the selector Sw. If Sw=0 the value X0 is copied to output Y; if Sw=1 the value X1 is copied to output Y, and so on. If the Sw input is outside the range 0 to (N-1), output Y is cleared.","The number of inputs N of this module is user-configurable in the range 1 - 16."],"tables":[]},{"name":"DateTime","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Current date and time","formula":"Returns current day and time","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Offs","input","Long","Offset","Optional offset input in seconds, added to the system time, e.g. for conversion between UTC and local time","0"],["D","output","Long","Day","Number of days since 1 Jan 1980","-"],["H","output","Int","Hour","Hour","-"],["M","output","Int","Minute","Minute","-"],["S","output","Int","Second","Second","-"],["DOW","output","Int","DayOfWeek","Day of week (=0..Monday, =1..Tuesday, ..., =6..Sunday)","-"],["SOD","output","Long","SecondOfDay","Seconds since midnight (0 - 86399)","-"]],"notes":["The module reads the configured PLC date and time and sets the corresponding output values. In the module configuration dialog the output pin SOD (seconds since midnight) and the input Offset can be enabled."],"tables":[]},{"name":"DecodeDate","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Decomposition of the date into day, month and year","formula":"Decodes the date value","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Date","input","Long","Date","Date as the number of days since 1 Jan 1980","0"],["Day","output","Int","Day","Day of month (1 - 31)","-"],["Mon","output","Int","Month","Month (1 - 12)","-"],["Year","output","Int","Year","Year (1980 - 2190)","-"],["MMDD","output","Int","Month-Day","Month and day (0101 - 1231)","-"]],"notes":["The module converts a date in integer form into its individual parts - day, month and year. The Date input can be connected to output D of the DateTime module. The value on output MMDD is given as 100*Month + Day. It can usefully be employed, for example, to detect public holidays in the year using the MCompare module."],"tables":[]},{"name":"EncodeDate","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Computation of the date from day, month and year","formula":"Encodes the date value","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Day","input","Int","Day","Day of month (1 - 31)","1"],["Mon","input","Int","Month","Month (1 - 12)","1"],["Year","input","Int","Year","Year (1980 - 2190)","2000"],["Date","output","Long","Date","Date as the number of days since 1 Jan 1980","-"]],"notes":["The module converts the individual parts of a date - day, month and year - into a date in integer form. Output Date has the same range as output D of the DateTime module."],"tables":[]},{"name":"PulseGen","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Pulse generator","formula":"Generates pulses","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Act","input","Boolean","Active","Enables pulse generation","0"],["TOn","parameter","Int","Time On","Pulse length in cycles","1"],["TOff","parameter","Int","Time Off","Time between pulses in cycles","1"],["Cnt","output","Int","Counter","Cycle counter","-"],["Out","output","Boolean","Output","Generated pulses","-"]],"notes":["If the Act input is active (=1), pulses of length TOn with an interval of TOff are generated on output Out. The values TOn and TOff are numbers of cycles. If the module is placed in the \"Timer 1s\" process these values are in seconds. Output Cnt acts as a cycle counter; when its value reaches or exceeds (e.g. after changing TOn or TOff) the sum TOn+TOff it is cleared. If Act=0 both outputs are cleared."],"tables":[]},{"name":"PulseLen","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Measures the pulse length","formula":"Measures length of pulse","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["In","input","Boolean","Input","Input","0"],["Len","output","Int","Length","Cycle counter","-"]],"notes":["The module measures the length of the pulse applied to input In. With the rising edge (transition from 0 to 1) on input In it starts counting process cycles into output Len. The counting stops when input In is cleared. The value on output Len is retained until the next pulse occurs."],"tables":[]},{"name":"SinglePulse","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Generates a pulse of the requested length","formula":"Generates single pulse","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Tr","input","Boolean","Trigger","Trigger","0"],["TOn","parameter","Int","Time On","Pulse length in cycles","1"],["Cnt","output","Int","Counter","Cycle counter","-"],["Out","output","Boolean","Output","Generated pulses","-"]],"notes":["If a rising edge (transition from 0 to 1) occurs on input Tr, output Out will be at logical 1 for TOn process cycles. Output Cnt serves as a pulse counter that takes the values 1 to TOn while the pulse is active. It is then cleared together with output Out."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Timer","category":"Main","group":"Timers","title":"Multi-function timer","formula":"Timer","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["In","input","Boolean","Input","Input signal. A 0-->1 edge starts the timing","0"],["Rst","input","Boolean","Reset","A logical 1 on the Reset input clears the timer","0"],["Dly","parameter","Int","Delay","Pulse length in cycles","1"],["Cnt","output","Int","Counter","Cycle counter","-"],["Out","output","Boolean","Output","Generated pulses","-"]],"notes":["The timer works in one of 4 modes, which are selected in the configuration dialog:","The Fixed Pulse and Truncated Pulse modes generate a pulse of the length Delay process cycles. In the Truncated Pulse mode the pulse is shortened if the input goes to level 0 during the timing.","In the On-Delay and On-Delay Continuous modes the input pulse is delayed by Delay process cycles. In On-Delay mode the output pulse ends when input In goes to 0. In On-Delay Continuous mode the output pulse ends only on the value 1 at the Reset input.","The Input and Output pins can be inverted.","In the idle state output Counter has the value 0; during timing it grows from 1 up to the value Delay."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Equitherm","category":"Thermostat","group":"","title":"Transformation according to the heating (equithermal) curve","formula":"Returns water temperature calculated by equitherm [AX, AY]-[BX, BY]","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["OT","input","Int","Outdoor Temperature","Outdoor temperature","0"],["AX","parameter","Int","X of Point A","Outdoor temperature for point A","0"],["AY","parameter","Int","Y of Point A","Required water temperature for point A","0"],["BX","parameter","Int","X of Point B","Outdoor temperature for point B","0"],["BY","parameter","Int","Y of Point B","Required water temperature for point B","0"],["WT","output","Int","Water Temperature","Required water temperature","-"]],"notes":["The module computes the required water temperature WT as a function of the outdoor temperature OT according to the heating (equithermal) curve defined by points A and B, i.e. the parameters AX, AY, BX and BY.","The course of the transformation is shown in the following graph."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Valve","category":"Thermostat","group":"","title":"Control of an analog valve","formula":"Prepares analog output for valve","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["Op","input","Boolean","Open","Open the valve","0"],["Cl","input","Boolean","Close","Close the valve","0"],["St","parameter","Int","Step","Step of change","1"],["Max","parameter","Int","Maximum","Maximum output value","0"],["Min","parameter","Int","Minimum","Minimum output value","0"],["Y","output","Int","Y","Output value","-"]],"notes":["The module sets the value of output Y according to a request to increase it (input Op) or decrease it (input Cl). If one of the inputs Op or Cl is active (=1), the output value is increased or decreased by the value St in every process cycle. If both inputs are 0, or both are 1, output Y does not change. The resulting value is also limited by the parameters Min and Max."],"tables":[]},{"name":"WaterRegulator","category":"Thermostat","group":"","title":"Temperature control of heating/chilling water","formula":"Water temperature comparator with insensibility band and hysteresis.","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["T","input","Int","Temperature","Actual temperature of the heating/chilling water","0"],["ReqT","parameter","Int","Required temperature","Required temperature of the heating/chilling water","0"],["InsensBand","parameter","Int","Insensitivity band","Dead band","0"],["HalfHyst","parameter","Int","Half hysteresis","Hysteresis half-width","0"],["Cooling","parameter","Boolean","Cooling","Mode (=0..heating, =1..cooling)","0"],["Op","output","Boolean","Open","Request to open the valve","-"],["Cl","output","Boolean","Close","Request to close the valve","-"]],"notes":["The module regulates the temperature of heating or chilling water and issues commands to open or close the mixing valve. In heating mode, when the Cooling input is 0, output Cl is activated when the temperature difference (T-ReqT)>(InsensBand+HalfHyst) and cleared when (T-ReqT)<(InsensBand-HalfHyst). Similarly output Op is activated when (T-ReqT)<(-InsensBand-HalfHyst) and cleared when (T-ReqT)>(-InsensBand+HalfHyst). In cooling mode (Cooling=1) the logic of outputs Op and Cl is reversed, i.e. opening is exchanged for closing.","The heating mode is shown in the following graph (IB means InsensBand, HH HalfHyst). For cooling, swap Op and Cl."],"tables":[]},{"name":"WeekProgram","category":"Thermostat","group":"","title":"Weekly temperature program","formula":"Returns value from week program","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the function (=0..not executed, =1..executed)","1"],["DOW","input","Int","Day of week","Day of week (=0..Monday, =1..Tuesday, ..., =6..Sunday)","0"],["H","input","Int","Hour","Hour","0"],["M","input","Int","Minute","Minute","0"],["T","output","Int","Temperature","Temperature according to the program","-"]],"notes":["The module writes the requested temperature for day DOW, hour H and minute M into output T according to the configured program. It is typically used together with the DateTime module","The weekly program is configured via the module configuration."],"tables":[]},{"name":"BoolVar","category":"Vars","group":"","title":"Virtual variable of type Bool","formula":"Variable of bool type","pins":[["Y","output","Bool","Y","Variable of type Bool","-"]],"notes":["The module performs no operation; it only allocates space for a variable of type Bool in the data block, thereby making it available over the D3Net protocol (e.g. for visualisation). This variable can also be used in the menu items of the P3Menu module or stored by the SaveData module."],"tables":[]},{"name":"FloatVar","category":"Vars","group":"","title":"Virtual variable of type Float","formula":"Variable of float type","pins":[["Y","output","Float","Y","Variable of type Float","-"]],"notes":["The module performs no operation; it only allocates space for a variable of type Float in the data block, thereby making it available over the D3Net protocol (e.g. for visualisation). This variable can also be used in the menu items of the P3Menu module or stored by the SaveData module."],"tables":[]},{"name":"IntVar","category":"Vars","group":"","title":"Virtual variable of type Int","formula":"Variable of int type","pins":[["Y","output","Int","Y","Variable of type Int","-"]],"notes":["The module performs no operation; it only allocates space for a variable of type Int in the data block, thereby making it available over the D3Net protocol (e.g. for visualisation). This variable can also be used in the menu items of the P3Menu module or stored by the SaveData module."],"tables":[]},{"name":"LongVar","category":"Vars","group":"","title":"Virtual variable of type Long","formula":"Variable of long type","pins":[["Y","output","Long","Y","Variable of type Long","-"]],"notes":["The module performs no operation; it only allocates space for a variable of type Long in the data block, thereby making it available over the D3Net protocol (e.g. for visualisation). This variable can also be used in the menu items of the P3Menu module or stored by the SaveData module."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Segment","category":"Visual","group":"","title":"Display of a seven-segment digit","formula":"Display 7-segment number","pins":[["En","input","Boolean","Enabled","Option to disable the display (=0..all segments off, =1..shown)","1"],["A","input","Boolean","Segment A","Top bar of the digit","0"],["B","input","Boolean","Segment B","Upper right bar","0"],["C","input","Boolean","Segment C","Lower right bar","0"],["D","input","Boolean","Segment D","Bottom bar","0"],["E","input","Boolean","Segment E","Lower left bar","0"],["F","input","Boolean","Segment F","Upper left bar","0"],["G","input","Boolean","Segment G","Middle bar","0"],["DP","input","Boolean","Decimal Point","The decimal point","0"]],"notes":["The module has nine inputs and no outputs. It draws one digit of a seven-segment display: a segment is lit while its input is 1, and with En = 0 all of them are off.","It is shown in the simulation and is not part of the program the PLC runs: the compiled program has no record for it, so it adds nothing to the table that is uploaded (the captured exports account for every other block and for neither display).","To show a number, drive the inputs from a decoder (for example an Int2Bits whose bits go through an ISwitch that selects each digit's segment pattern, as the *Int2Seg macro of kostka 1.pcc does) and wire the segment outputs to the A to G inputs.","On a real board the segments are ordinary digital outputs: the tutorial Duino_7segm01_EDU.pdf lists A, B and C on outputs 11, 12 and 13, D and E on 2 and 3, F and G on 7 and 8 and the decimal point on 10, with output 9 multiplexing the digits."],"tables":[]},{"name":"Value","category":"Visual","group":"","title":"Display of a numeric value","formula":"Display Value","pins":[["X","input","Float","Vstup","Input of the displayed value","0"]],"notes":["The module is used to display the value connected to input X in simulation or program-watch (Watch) mode. It has no effect on the resulting program in the PLC."],"tables":[]}]}
